  "blocks": {
    "\"Claude Code locally, Cursor for the UI work — same model underneath, different harnesses.\"": "“本地工作用 Claude Code，UI 工作用 Cursor——底层是同一个模型，但运行框架不同。”",
    "\"Which agent are you using for the migration?\"": "“这次迁移你在用哪个智能体？”",
    "A model harnessed with tools, a system prompt, and a context window, that takes turns with a user. Claude Code is an agent. Cursor is an agent. Claude.ai is an agent. An agent is what you actually talk to — it's the model in motion, configured for a purpose.": "智能体是一个被<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/tool\">工具</a>、<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/system-prompt\">系统提示词</a>和<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-window\">上下文窗口</a>组织起来，并与用户轮流交互的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/model\">模型</a>。Claude Code 是智能体，Cursor 是智能体，Claude.ai 也是智能体。你真正与之对话的是智能体——也就是为特定目的配置好、正在运行中的模型。",
    "Avoid: \"the AI\", \"the bot\" (too vague — they hide whether you mean the parameters or the harnessed thing).": "<em>避免：</em>说“那个 AI”或“那个机器人”（过于含糊，会掩盖你指的是参数本身，还是被运行框架组织起来的整体）。",
    "The idea is older than this wave of AI. Software agents — programs you delegate a goal to, which act on your behalf — have been a concept for as long as AI has.": "这个概念比当前这波 AI 热潮更早。软件智能体——接受你委托的目标并代表你行动的程序——几乎从 AI 概念诞生之初就已经存在。",
    "Unlike most terms in this dictionary, \"agent\" doesn't name a mechanical part. The model is a file of parameters; the harness is software you can point at. The agent is neither — it's the unit you're speaking to. People anthropomorphize AI constantly, and the agent is the anthropomorphized unit: the thing you delegate to, the thing that reads your message and answers, the \"it\" in \"it broke the build again\". When you say the agent did something, you mean the model-plus-harness did it, but you're addressing the combination as a single actor.": "与本词典中的大多数术语不同，“智能体”并不指某个机械部件。模型是一份参数文件；<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/harness\">运行框架</a>是可以明确指认的软件；智能体则两者都不是——它是你正在交谈的那个单位。人们经常把 AI 拟人化，而智能体就是被拟人化的单位：你把任务委托给它，它读取你的消息并作答，也是“它又把构建弄坏了”中的那个“它”。当你说智能体做了某件事时，实际指的是模型与运行框架共同完成了这件事，但你把这个组合当成单一行动者来称呼。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
  },
